{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticProductRecurrence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticProductRecurrence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticProductRecurrence.e1_lattice_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticProductRecurrence.e1_lattice_sum","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticProductRecurrence.lean#L83-L94","doc":"**Explicit `x¹`-coefficient (the `e_1` telescope).** The first tetraplectic\nsymmetric function `e_1` over the finite lattice is the geometric sum\n`∑_{n<N} q^{2n+1}`; here in cleared form `(q² − 1)·∑_{n<N} q^{2n+1} = q^{2N+1} − q`,\nthe `N→∞` limit of which is `q/(1−q²) = q^{1²}/(q²;q²)_1`, the `k=1` closed form.\nProved by induction on `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticProductRecurrence.tetraProd_funcEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticProductRecurrence.tetraProd_funcEq","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticProductRecurrence.lean#L59-L81","doc":"**The q²-dilation functional equation of the tetraplectic product.**\n`(1 + q x) · P_N(q² x) = (1 + q^{2N+1} x) · P_N(x)`. Both sides equal `P_{N+1}(x)`:\nthe left factors `(1+qx)` back in as the `n=0` term after the `q²`-dilation reindexes\n`n ↦ n+1`; the right appends the `n=N` term. This is the recurrence that pins the\n`q^{k²}/(q²;q²)_k` coefficients of the reduction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticProductRecurrence.tetraProd_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticProductRecurrence.tetraProd_succ","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticProductRecurrence.lean#L55-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticProductRecurrence.tetraProd_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticProductRecurrence.tetraProd_zero","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticProductRecurrence.lean#L52-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticProductRecurrence.tetraProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticProductRecurrence.tetraProd","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticProductRecurrence.lean#L47-L50","doc":"The finite tetraplectic single-lattice product\n`P_N(x) = ∏_{n=0}^{N-1} (1 + q^{2n+1} x)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}